 "What is the most likely diagnosis?",
 "Neuroleptic malignant syndrome",
 ["Serotonin syndrome with hyperreflexia and clonus as the better fit","Lethal catatonia without a drug history","Thyroid storm with a normal thyroid examination and no history","Malignant hyperthermia in the community without anaesthetic trigger"],
 "NMS: rigidity, fever, autonomic instability, and raised CK after dopamine blockade. Stop antipsychotics, support, and consider bromocriptine/dantrolene/ECT in severe cases.",
 ["Serotonin syndrome is hyperreflexic with clonus, usually on serotonergic drugs.","Catatonia can overlap but the drug trigger and CK point to NMS.","No thyroid features.","MH is anaesthetic-triggered."],
